<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  The app's privacy manifest (docs/release/APP_STORE_HANDOFF.md §3.1). It must say what the App Privacy answers in
  App Store Connect say (D8), and both must follow what the code sends (handoff §6). It describes the App Store build
  (`npm run build:store`), which has no Ask: nothing is sent to Anthropic, so Other User Content is not collected
  (release decision D8).

  - No tracking, no tracking domains: no analytics, ads, crash reporting or accounts of ours. The App Store build is
    the OAuth flavour (`build:store` sets VITE_AG_CONNECT=oauth): searches go to seats.aero with the access token from
    seats.aero's own sign-in, and the one other host is the token service at awardgrid.dowhiz.com (sites/auth), which
    exchanges and refreshes the sign-in tokens and keeps nothing it receives, so it collects nothing (plan 47F step 6).
  - Collected, linked to the user, for app functionality only: Search History (the search parameters sent to
    seats.aero).
  - Required-reason APIs: file timestamps (C617.1, files inside the app container), from IONFilesystemLib under
    @capacitor/filesystem, which ships no manifest of its own. Capacitor and CapacitorCordova carry their own
    manifests; KeychainSwift uses no required-reason API.
-->
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeSearchHistory</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeLinked</key>
			<true/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeTracking</key>
			<false/>
			<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposes</key>
			<array>
				<string>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypePurposeAppFunctionality</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
